<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:svg="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:ns3="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:db="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.0-subset Scilab" xml:id="gf_poly_subtract" xml:lang="en">

    <refnamediv>
        <refname>gf_poly_subtract</refname>
        <refpurpose>Subtracts polynomials over GF(p)</refpurpose>
    </refnamediv>
    <refsynopsisdiv>
        <title>Syntax</title>
        <synopsis>c = gf_poly_subtract(a, b, p)</synopsis>
    </refsynopsisdiv>
    <refsection>
        <title>Arguments</title>
        <variablelist>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>a, b</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>Polynomial over GF(p): a row vector of integer coefficients in 0 .. p-1, constant term first. For instance <literal>[1 0 1 1]</literal> is 1 + x² + x³. The two polynomials can have different lengths.</para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>p</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>Prime number: the characteristic of the field.</para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>c</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>Result as a row of coefficients, constant term first, trimmed to its degree (no trailing zeros). The zero polynomial is returned as <literal>0</literal>.</para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
        </variablelist>
    </refsection>
    <refsection>
        <title>Description</title>
        <para><literal>gf_poly_subtract(a, b, p)</literal> computes a - b, subtracting coefficients of equal degree modulo p.</para>
    </refsection>
    <refsection>
        <title>Examples</title>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
gf_poly_subtract([1 2], [0 0 1], 3)   // [1 2 2]: (1 + 2x) - x^2 = 1 + 2x + 2x^2
]]></programlisting>
    </refsection>
    <refsection role="see also">
        <title>See also</title>
        <simplelist type="inline">
            <member><link linkend="gf_poly_add">gf_poly_add</link></member>
            <member><link linkend="gf_subtract">gf_subtract</link></member>
        </simplelist>
    </refsection>
    <refsection role="history">
        <title>History</title>
